WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.970
- On The Daily Wire, you
talked about one problem

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:06.270
with our culture is that
we worship celebrities,

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.410
but earlier, when you waved to our table,

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.684
I'm pretty sure everyone
was about to faint.

00:00:10.684 --> 00:00:11.517
(audience laughs)

00:00:11.517 --> 00:00:14.724
Do you think that worshiping celebrities

00:00:14.724 --> 00:00:16.774
in a conservative setting has almost been

00:00:16.774 --> 00:00:19.490
a positive thing for
spurring the movement?

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:21.470
- Well, what I always hope
is the reason that people

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:23.270
like myself is because they like my stuff.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.960
They like how I think and they
like how I express arguments.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.020
None of you know me personally.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.913
For all you know, I
could be an ax murderer.

00:00:28.913 --> 00:00:29.746
(audience laughs)

00:00:29.746 --> 00:00:31.004
So, when it comes to--I'm not.

00:00:31.004 --> 00:00:34.034
But when it comes to celebrity worship,

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.710
my problem is not you liking something

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:37.700
somebody says or what they do.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.608
If you wanna be a big Chris
Pratt fan 'cause you think

00:00:39.608 --> 00:00:41.563
he's a great actor or you wanna be

00:00:41.563 --> 00:00:44.750
and by the way his message to
the MTV Awards was fantastic.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.110
Or if you wanna be a fan
of what he said there,

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:47.970
I think that's great.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.580
What I don't like is when we
start extending the worship

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.260
of celebrity into areas where

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.640
celebrities have no business being.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:55.473
I don't care,

00:00:55.473 --> 00:00:57.760
I'm glad that Kanye West
said that he's open-minded,

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.150
but I frankly do not care
very much about Kanye West's

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:03.430
opinion on politics because I
don't think he knows anything.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.340
And I don't really care
what Kim Kardashian

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.060
has to say about pardons for drug dealers

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.480
'cause I don't think she knows anything.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:09.410
If she wants to bring an expert in

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:10.570
to meet the President and talk about it,

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:11.403
that's one thing,

00:01:11.403 --> 00:01:12.330
but we have a tendency

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:13.798
in our culture to worship celebrities,

00:01:13.798 --> 00:01:15.660
not for the things that they are good at,

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:16.930
which I think is,

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:18.320
I don't like the word worship,

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:20.530
but to like celebrities
or look up to celebrities

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:21.993
for the things that they're
good at, that's fine.

00:01:21.993 --> 00:01:23.344
When I was growing up, I was a violinist.

00:01:23.344 --> 00:01:24.743
I was a classically trained,

00:01:24.743 --> 00:01:27.385
basically concert level violinist

00:01:27.385 --> 00:01:30.360
and I used to idolize Jascha Heifetz.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.090
He's the greatest violinist in history

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.720
and I didn't idolize him

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.170
for his set of personal interactions,

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.420
I idolized him because
he's a great violinist.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.370
I think that's totally
normal and totally fine.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.360
I think it's another thing
to say that celebrities

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:41.340
know things that they do not,

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.605
so if you're looking to
me for basketball tips,

00:01:42.605 --> 00:01:44.710
I would say that that's a waste of time.

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:45.930
If you're looking to me for books to read,

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:48.230
I think that's a pretty
good use of your time.

